    "description": "ShippingQuoteService.quote currently combines cart validation, warehouse distance lookup, carrier filtering, zone-rate selection, fuel surcharge calculation, tax calculation, discount application, currency rounding, and response assembly in one long method. Loop indices, temporary rate tables, condition branches, and formatting details are mixed with the high-level pricing policy, so reviewers must reconstruct the entire calculation before changing one rule. The platform team needs each pricing concern to change and test independently, but the public quote operation must still read from validation through final presentation. Refactor the method into short named operations that remain at the same conceptual level, such as validateCart, selectEligibleCarriers, chooseZoneRate, applySurcharges, applyDiscounts, roundMonetaryAmount, and assembleQuote. Helpers should receive and return clear domain values rather than sharing mutable controller state, and the orchestration method should contain only the ordered calls.",
    "decision_statement": "Determine how ShippingQuoteService.quote should be divided so pricing policy is readable top-down and each concern can evolve independently.",
    "notes": "composed-method fits the quote operation refactored into same-level named steps with value-passing helpers; macro-method and method-object are near misses for the call-only outline and shared-state decomposition, with inline-message supporting intention-revealing step names."
  },
